   "description": "Fibo 2.0 Edit is Bria's image editing model for background changes, product restaging, campaign adaptations, and reference-guided variations. Bria states that the model is trained on licensed data.\n\nThe endpoint accepts one to four images in image_urls: the source image first, followed by up to three references. Instructions can refer to them as <image_1>, <image_2>, and so on. Free-form instructions are expanded into a VGL document, which is returned with the edited image and can be reused directly.\n\nSingle-image requests keep the source aspect ratio. An optional mask marks the area to regenerate in white and the area to preserve in black; it must match the source image size. Masked output retains the source dimensions and the original pixels outside the mask. Masks are supported only with a single image.\n\nMulti-image requests support 21 output aspect ratios at approximately one megapixel. Left unset, the output keeps the first image's aspect ratio. A seed controls reproducibility, and sync mode returns the image directly in the response.\n\nFor generation from a text prompt, use Fibo 2.0 Generate.",
   "authSkippable": false,
